        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(cli): use formatErrorMessage for structured error output in skills and update commands",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe `skills-cli.ts` and `update-cli.ts` CLI command handlers both format caught errors with `String(err)`, which discards error cause chains. Other CLI files in the same directory (`acp-cli.ts`, `gateway-cli/run.ts`, `ports.ts`, `plugins-search-command.ts`) already import and use `formatErrorMessage(err)` from `src/infra/errors.ts` for structured error presentation.\n\n**Before:** `String(err)` — loses cause info:\n```\nError: Failed to fetch skill catalog\n```\n\n**After:** `formatErrorMessage(err)` — preserves cause chain:\n```\nFailed to fetch skill catalog | Connection refused\n```\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- **Behavior or issue addressed**: `String(err)` → `formatErrorMessage(err)` for consistent structured error output in `skills-cli.ts` (13 sites) and `update-cli.ts` (4 sites)\n- **Real environment tested**: Node 22.22, Linux x86_64, local dev checkout\n- **Exact steps or command run after this patch**: `node --import tsx proof-97830.mjs` creating a structured error with cause chain, comparing `String(err)` vs `formatErrorMessage(err)` output\n- **Evidence after fix**:\n  ```\n  === PR #97830 proof ===\n\n  --- String(err) output (BEFORE) ---\n  Error: Failed to fetch skill catalog\n\n  --- formatErrorMessage(err) output (AFTER) ---\n  Failed to fetch skill catalog | Connection refused\n  ```\n- **Observed result after fix**: `formatErrorMessage` preserves the cause chain (`Connection refused`) that `String()` silently drops. 188/188 CLI tests pass.\n- **What was not tested**: Live CLI invocation of each skill/update subcommand with forced error conditions\n\n## Files Changed\n\n| File | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `src/cli/skills-cli.ts` | Added `formatErrorMessage` import; replaced 13 `String(err)` |\n| `src/cli/update-cli.ts` | Added `formatErrorMessage` import; replaced 4 `String(err)` |\n\nGenerated with Claude Code",
